  "limits": [
    "Random-window exhausts a shuffled bounded window from the lowest missing endpoints before advancing. Window size 1 is sequential; selection is not globally uniform or sampling with replacement.",
    "Seed is a 256-bit hexadecimal value (default zero); window size is 1..256 tiles (default 64). Both overrides require random-window.",
    "SHA-256 domain/seed/counter bytes and masked rejection draws define portable descending Fisher-Yates. The ordering seed is not a security key or a performance promise.",
    "Work units are partitioned at window creation, clipped to saved gaps/window bounds. Adaptive sizing changes apply to the next window. At most W tile records and W active owners exist beyond the input gaps.",
    "Overflow and partial target groups retain the selected tile. All-target completion and CPU verification precede coverage; replay deduplicates saved matches.",
    "Restart rebuilds missing coverage and resets the stream. Seed, window, geometry and policy may change; sequence reproducibility requires identical initial gaps, geometry and work sizes.",
    "Job/configuration/table identity, schema 7, protocol, receipts and capabilities are unchanged. Old BSGS workers can resume forward; scalar order and coordinator block claims are separate.",
    "Both kernels tested on HIP/CUDA; group-8 spots cover eight ordinals. No exhaustive kernel-by-device product, fleet scaling or new partition claim.",
    "Eleven focused host sanitizer gates; no whole-application or device-code sanitizer coverage claim.",
    "No new device arithmetic or throughput claim. Other families\u2019 random traversal remains pending in C23.",
    "Public fixtures only; no enrollment credentials or journal databases archived."
  ],
